"""Replace a legacy sandbox bootstrap after a proved whole-sandbox stop.

Private inventory: common project/env_file/runtime_image/docker_context and units
runner/keeper, plus sandbox:{name, clone_path, known_files, receipts_path,
script_path, profile_path, profile_source, systemd_user_dir, evidence_dir,
remote_ref, remote_name, declared_remote, declaration_files, release_image,
expected_sbx_version, legacy_dropins, legacy_command_markers, forbidden_values}.
Routes come ONLY from the explicit env file: FACTORY_GATEWAY_ADDRESS,
FORGE_TARGET_OWNER_URL, FORGE_SANDBOX_SIDECAR_URL, FORGE_SANDBOX_RUNNER_URL.
The producer profile retains all choices except gateway publish addresses,
explicit allow-rule replacements, receipts_path and cwd. sandbox.allow_replacements
maps old host:port entries to env variable NAMES holding replacement host:port.
No shell sourcing, ambient route overrides or broker clients.
"""
